sequenceDiagram
    title In-Store Cart-Bridge: Associate scans loyalty QR at POS

    participant POS as POS Client
    participant GW as Apollo Gateway
    participant ID as Identity Service
    participant CART as Cart Service
    participant CACHE as Inventory Cache (Redis)
    participant SAP as SAP ECC
    participant DB as Order Database

    Note over POS,SAP: Happy path p95 target: < 1500ms total (in-store cart hydration budget)

    POS->>GW: POST /graphql { cartMerge(loyaltyQR: "...") } [~15ms gateway routing]
    GW->>ID: validateToken(loyaltyQR) [~10ms local Redis session check]
    ID-->>GW: { customerId, sessionValid: true } [~10ms]

    GW->>CART: getCart(customerId) [~10ms service call]
    CART->>DB: SELECT cart_items WHERE customer_id = ? [~15ms PostgreSQL p95]
    DB-->>CART: [{ sku: "SKU-001", qty: 1 }, { sku: "SKU-042", qty: 2 }, { sku: "SKU-117", qty: 1 }]
    CART-->>GW: cart { lineItems: [...3 items...] } [~10ms]

    loop Per line item — 3 items, sequential (p95 volume)
        GW->>CACHE: GET stock:{storeId}:{sku} [~2ms Redis]
        alt Cache hit (p95: 85% of lookups)
            CACHE-->>GW: { confidence: 0.82, freshness_min: 12, available: true } [~2ms]
        else Cache miss (p95: 15% of lookups — triggers SAP inline fallback)
            Note over GW,SAP: Cache miss: SAP ECC inline query — +400ms p95
            GW->>SAP: RFC_READ_STOCK(sku, storeId) [~400ms SAP ECC round-trip]
            SAP-->>GW: { qty: 3, last_updated: "..." } [~400ms]
            GW->>CACHE: SET stock:{storeId}:{sku} EX 1800 [async write-back, ~2ms]
        end
    end

    GW-->>POS: { cart: { lineItems: [...], availabilityStates: [...] } } [~20ms serialisation]

    Note over POS,SAP: Happy path (all cache hits): ~82ms total
    Note over POS,SAP: Worst case (all 3 items cache-miss): ~82ms + (3 × 400ms) = ~1282ms — within 1500ms budget
    Note over POS,SAP: ---
    Note over POS,SAP: BOTTLENECK: SAP ECC inline lookup at ~400ms p95 dominates when inventory cache misses.
    Note over POS,SAP: Primary mitigation: cache warm-up on Kafka stock events (reduce miss rate to < 5%).
    Note over POS,SAP: Secondary mitigation: degrade to "stock unknown — confirm with floor staff" on SAP timeout > 1s.
